<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">29 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 29 August, from 1526 to 2005.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1526</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Suleiman the Magnificent crushes Hungary at Mohács</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Ottoman army destroyed the Hungarian forces at Mohács; King Louis II drowned while fleeing. Hungary was partitioned, and the Habsburgs inherited its crown.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suleiman-the-magnificent">Suleiman the Magnificent</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1842</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Treaty of Nanking ends the First Opium War</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">China ceded Hong Kong Island to Britain, opened five ports to foreign trade and paid a large indemnity. It was the first of the 'unequal treaties' China remembers as a century of humiliation.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-opium-war">First Opium War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong">Hong Kong</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1949</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Soviet Union tests its first atomic bomb</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The USSR exploded its first atomic bomb at Semipalatinsk in Kazakhstan, years earlier than the West expected. The American nuclear monopoly was over and the arms race had begun.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1966</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Beatles play their last concert for paying fans</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Beatles played a half-hour set at Candlestick Park in San Francisco. They then gave up touring to concentrate on studio albums such as Sgt. Pepper's Lonely Hearts Club Band.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepper">Pepper</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">2005</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hurricane Katrina strikes the US Gulf Coast</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Katrina made landfall as a Category 3 hurricane; storm surge broke the levees of New Orleans and flooded some 80 per cent of the city. More than 1,300 people died and the government response was widely condemned.</p></li></ol>
